[38;2;124;124;124mThe question: is such an operator compact?[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe key theorem here is: For a normal operator (or self-adjoint operator) on a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mHilbert space with a complete orthonormal system of eigenvectors {e_i} and [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcorresponding eigenvalues {λ_i}, the operator is compact if and only if λ_i → 0.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about this more carefully. The spectral theorem for compact self-[0m
[38;2;124;124;124madjoint operators says: A self-adjoint operator T on a Hilbert space H is [0m
